1
00:05:42,352 --> 00:05:48,352
20,000 Days on Earth is a documentary, drama,
music film directed by Jane Pollard.

2
00:11:24,705 --> 00:11:30,705
A semi-fictionalized documentary about a day in the life of
Australian musician Nick Cave's persona.

3
00:17:07,058 --> 00:17:13,058
Self, played by Nick Cave.

4
00:22:49,411 --> 00:22:55,411
Self, played by Warren Ellis.

5
00:28:31,764 --> 00:28:37,764
Self, played by Blixa Bargeld.

6
00:34:14,117 --> 00:34:20,117
Self, played by Susie Bick.

7
00:39:56,470 --> 00:40:02,470
Self, played by Arthur Cave.

8
00:45:38,823 --> 00:45:44,823
Self, played by Earl Cave.

9
00:51:21,176 --> 00:51:27,176
20,000 Days on Earth is a 2014 British musical documentary
drama film
co-written and directed by Iain Forsyth and Jane Pollard.

10
00:57:03,529 --> 00:57:09,529
Nick Cave also co-wrote the script with Forsyth and Pollard.

11
01:02:45,882 --> 01:02:51,882
The film premiered in-competition in the World Cinema Documentary
Competition at 2014 Sundance Film Festival on 20 January 2014.

12
01:08:28,235 --> 01:08:34,235
It won two Awards at the festival.

13
01:14:10,588 --> 01:14:16,588
After its premiere at Sundance Film Festival, Drafthouse
Films acquired distribution rights of the film.

14
01:19:52,941 --> 01:19:58,941
The film released on 17 September 2014 in United States.

15
01:25:35,294 --> 01:25:41,294
The film explores themes of docudrama, woman director, part fiction.

16
01:31:17,647 --> 01:31:23,647
The tone is emotional.
